{"chunk_id": "8209ee61ea08", "text": "Bhishma recounts the miraculous birth and early life of Suka, the son of the sage Vyasa (Krishna Dvaipayana). After Vyasa receives a boon from Shiva promising a supremely pure son, he encounters the apsara Ghritachi in the forest and is overcome with desire. Though he tries to restrain himself, his seed falls while he is kindling fire with sacrificial sticks, and from those very sticks the radiant child Suka is born. The event is marked by cosmic celebration: gods, rivers, and celestial beings honor the newborn sage, who already embodies Vedic wisdom. Suka quickly masters sacred knowledge, practices severe austerities, and becomes devoted to the path of liberation. Seeking final truth, he asks his father about emancipation, and Vyasa sends him to learn from King Janaka, emphasizing humility, discipline, and freedom from worldly attachments.\nVyasa\u2019s son Suka is miraculously born, revered by gods, masters sacred knowledge, and seeks the path of emancipation under guidance from his father and King Janaka.\nThemes: miraculous birth, asceticism, spiritual knowledge, detachment, quest for liberation", "vector": [0.02206888422369957, -0.007564952597022057, 0.005587143823504448, -0.015236454084515572, -0.03827759623527527, 0.01732747070491314, -0.020483974367380142, 0.0010122120147570968, -0.01909884251654148, -0.028714856132864952, 0.005743637215346098, 0.004325208254158497, 0.0005964225856587291, 0.00738515192642808, 0.0011953423963859677, -0.009123226627707481, 0.04126095771789551, -0.014450658112764359, 0.005174268037080765, -0.02407998964190483, -0.0025854690466076136, 0.006852408871054649, 0.01073477417230606, 0.011713690124452114, -0.028208749368786812, 0.024253131821751595, 0.009589376859366894, -0.019991187378764153, 0.006609344854950905, -0.018992293626070023, -0.013558313250541687, -0.006352961994707584, 0.00021934034884907305, 0.0036060051061213017, -0.03303007408976555, -0.0013193717459216714, -0.013718136586248875, -